-- title:
--   Level-field descent of the rigid level-q model, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring $A\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ the notation $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ stands for the Lean term `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`. The subalgebra $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` of $K_\ell$ is by definition the set of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, and `jChartFin` is $j_\ell$ viewed inside $C$.
--
--   **Level and constant data.** A prime $q$ with $q=2$ (`hq2`); a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`); a subgroup $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ equal to the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) (the kernel of the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` out of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ attached to `dvd_sq_mul q M'`) with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$ (`hH₁`); an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi$ (`hξ`); an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ equal to `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, the $k_0$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ (`hKℓ`), together with a nonzero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ (`hjℓ`), and the element `jqNModC k₀ q` of $k_0((\mathsf q))$ is assumed to lie in $K_\ell$ (`hjK`). Auxiliary data carried along: a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`), and $\zeta_0\in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`).
--
--   **The valuation subring and its reduction.** A valuation subring $A\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (`hA`, i.e. `A.LiesOverPrime q`); an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`) such that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`) and with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`). Elements $\varpi_t\in k_0$ with $\varpi_t\in A$ (`hϖtA`) and $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`); $\varpi_t'\in A_0$ with the same image as $\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`); an integer $m\ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'\cdot(\text{unit})$ in $A_0$ (`hm1`, `hm`). An intermediate field $K_b$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`), a valuation subring $A_b\subseteq K_b$ cut out by $A$ (`hAb`) whose maximal ideal is generated by a nonzero $\varpi_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`); and the tameness hypothesis that the image of $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$ (`htame`).
--
--   **The supersingular place downstairs.** A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ which is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places (`hW`), with a chosen $s\in W$; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-base change of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) in `fieldBar q M'`; and a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is, a valuation subring of integers with a surjective residue map onto the target, a map on places, and the compatibilities recorded in `ConstantReduction`. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0$`.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The chart and the point $y$.** A maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ (`hy`) containing the image of $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`), such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$ the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, the set of $j\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$ (`hss`). The hypothesis `hover` is the dictionary between $y$ and the place $s$: for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-base change lies in $R_0$`.integers`, has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which `jq` has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every realisation of the coefficientwise image of $g$ as an element of $K_\ell$ lying in $C$, and every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` states that any maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying that same dictionary is in the orbit of $y$: there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and an automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` (the $q$-expansion characterisation of the level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$) such that $\tau$ preserves $C$ and, for $f\in C$, $f\in y$ if and only if $\tau f\in y'$. Finally `hjC` places `jqNModC k₀ q` in $C$, and `ha₀y` asserts that it is congruent to (the image of) $a_0\in A_0$ modulo $y$.
--
--   **The affine model (`hS1`).** A subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ over $A_0$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t\subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` is a conjunction of thirteen clauses (summarised here): $C\subseteq B_t$ and $B_t$ has fraction field $K_\ell$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$ and its fibre modulo $\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal, and induces $y$ on $C$; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A₀)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the functions vanishing at $W_t$, compatible with scalars, and equivariant for every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) and an element of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) whose second coordinate $c$ is nontrivial for nontrivial $\tau$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$, together with a companion level automorphism realising the same $c$ with trivial matrix part; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is the image under some level automorphism of the one cut out by $W_t$; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose level translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Deck transformation and width (`hn1`, `hnq`, `hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`, `hζc`, `hζcprim`, `hn`).** An integer $n$ with $1\le n$ and $n\mid q+1$, equal to `placeWidthChar q M' s`; an element $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ attached to $\gamma_0^{-1}$ in the above sense, preserving $W_t$; and an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^n=1$ and $\zeta_c^k-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$.
--
--   **The ends (`hR7`), and the separation clauses (`hR9`, `hR10`).** A finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. The hypothesis `hR7` is a conjunction of twelve clauses (summarised here): $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while no smaller positive power does, and every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements, the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ permute `ends` transitively, $\tau_0$ preserves each end, and distinct ends are separated by a function that is a nonunit in one and a unit in the other; there is a level-stable $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$ of finite type contained in every end and presenting each end as a localisation of it; a level automorphism carrying an end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and noetherian, contains $C$, meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$ and has residue field generated by the constants, and its adic completion is identified with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$ by an isomorphism $\iota$ matching constants, sending two elements $c_x,c_y\in O$ with $c_x c_y=\pi_0^m\cdot(\text{unit})$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$ respectively, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, sending `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ to a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$, and conjugating $\tau_0$ into an automorphism $\theta_0$ with $\theta_0(U)\equiv\zeta_c U$ and $\theta_0(V)\equiv\zeta_c^{-1}V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each end moreover carries a discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ dominating it, meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, with uniformiser $\pi_0$, containing $C$, inducing $y$ on $C$ in a sharp form, annihilating no polynomial congruence for a parameter $t$ or for `jqNModC k₀ q`, and detecting $O$ among the ends, and a level-stable finite-type subalgebra $B_x\subseteq B_t\cap O$ with poles only where $j_\ell$ has poles, presenting $O$ as its localisation and containing an element detecting non-integrality of $j_\ell$; and finally every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, containing $C$ and inducing $y$ on $C$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends. The hypothesis `hR9` provides an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ that meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and for which $j_\ell$ satisfies no monic integral congruence; `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ that is not in the level orbit of $y$, an element of $B_t$ separating $y''$ from the corresponding valuation subrings.
--
--   **The descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by all $\tau$ for which there is $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$ (`hB₀`); and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ induced by $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give `fieldBar q M'` its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ with the property that an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ precisely when every Laurent coefficient of $f$ is the image of an element of $k_0$, there exists an isomorphism of $k_0$-algebras $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }F_0$ such that:
--
--   1.
--
--   (coefficient law) for every $f\in K_0$, the coefficientwise image under $k_0\hookrightarrow\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the Laurent series of $f$ equals the Laurent series of $\varphi(f)$;
--
--   2.
--
--   (level-automorphism dictionary) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, that is, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, and every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi'\in k_0$ whose image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is $\zeta$, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau:K_\ell\xrightarrow{\sim}K_\ell$ over $k_0$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ' q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ` — the level automorphism attached to $\gamma$ itself, not to $\gamma^{-1}$ as in the definition of $G$ — the map $\tau$ carries $K_0$ into $K_0$, and for every $f\in K_0$ one has $\varphi(\tau f)=$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $(\varphi(f))$, where `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the chosen $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` satisfying the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ`;
--
--   3.
--
--   (level-$M'$ functions) for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, the value of $\varphi$ on it is the image under the inclusion `hle` of the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-base change of $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`.
--
--   This is the descent step of the $q=2$ construction in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ diamond frame: the fixed field of the group generated by the level automorphisms for $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ inside the rigid level-$q$ function field $K_\ell$ is identified, compatibly with $q$-expansions, with the level field $F_0$ cut out inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(\Gamma_{H}(q^2M'))$ by the condition that all Laurent coefficients be constants from $k_0$, and the level action upstairs is matched with `levelAutBar` downstairs. It is obtained by combining the existence statement for $\varphi$ with the dictionary for the level automorphisms, and it feeds the assembled supersingular discrete-valuation-ring and affine-chart statement for the semistable model at $q$.
